#: source/store/index.md:1
msgid "Nix Store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:3
msgid ""
"The _Nix store_ is an abstraction to store immutable file system data (such "
"as software packages) that can have dependencies on other such data."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:5
msgid ""
"Concretely, albeit using concepts that are only defined in the rest of the "
"chapter, a store consists of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:7
msgid ""
"A set of [store objects](./store-object.md), the immutable file system data."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:9
msgid ""
"This can also be looked at as a map from [store paths](./store-path.md) to "
"store objects."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:11
msgid ""
"A set of [derivations](./derivation/index.md), instructions for building "
"store objects."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:13
msgid ""
"This can also be looked at as a map from [store paths](./store-path.md) to "
"derivations. Since store paths to derivations always end in `.drv`, and "
"store paths to other store objects never do, the two maps can also be "
"combined into one. Derivations can also be encoded as store objects too."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:17
msgid ""
"A [build trace](./build-trace.md), a record of which derivations have been "
"built and what they produced."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:19
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:21
msgid ""
"The concept of a build trace is currently [**experimental**](../development/"
"experimental-features.md#xp-feature-ca-derivations) and subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/index.md:25
msgid ""
"There are [multiple types of Nix stores](./types/index.md) with different "
"capabilities, such as the default one on the [local file system](./types/"
"local-store.md) (`/nix/store`) or [binary caches](./types/http-binary-cache-"
"store.md)."
msgstr ""
